      "before": "a1-u03-d08-e01",
      "title": { "en": "Babcia and dziadek" },
      "body": { "en": "*Babcia*, grandma, ends in *-a*: *moja babcia*. *Dziadek*, grandpa, ends in a consonant: *mój dziadek*." }
    },
    {
      "id": "a1-u03-d08-t02",
      "before": "a1-u03-d08-e06",
      "title": { "en": "Mam brata, mam siostrę" },
      "body": { "en": "After *mam*, *masz*, *ma* and the other forms of *mieć*, the person you have changes ending. *Brat* gives *brata* and *syn* gives *syna*; *siostra* gives *siostrę* and *córka* gives *córkę*. Neuter words stay as they are: *mam dziecko*, *mam rodzeństwo*. Other family words change too, so for now use only these four; Unit 5 explains the ending." }
    }
  ],
